[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3641066863","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113881#issuecomment-3641066863","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113881","id":3641066863,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZBkVv","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T09:36:22Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T09:37:02Z","body":"The change from 4.4 is probably from:\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107595\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107618\n\nThe resulting quaternion from this operation is undefined, or rather there's an infinite number of them, the resulting value is picked from that infinite number\n\nHowever the specific behavior in this case should be documented ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3641066863/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643617062","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113881#issuecomment-3643617062","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113881","id":3643617062,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZLS8m","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T20:13:33Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T20:13:33Z","body":"Is this a C#-specific issue? I don't have a .NET environment, so I can't verify. But for GDScript, the result is as follows:\n\n```GDScript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprint(\"Back->Forward:\" + str(Quaternion(Vector3.BACK, Vector3.FORWARD).get_euler()))\n\tprint(\"Forward->Back:\" + str(Quaternion(Vector3.FORWARD, Vector3.BACK).get_euler()))\n\n\tprint(\"Forward->Right:\" + str(Quaternion(Vector3.FORWARD, Vector3.RIGHT).get_euler()))\n\tprint(\"Forward->Back:\" + str(Quaternion(Vector3.FORWARD, Vector3.BACK).get_euler()))\n\n\tprint(\"Forward->Up:\" + str(Quaternion(Vector3.FORWARD, Vector3.UP).get_euler()))\n\tprint(\"Forward->Back:\" + str(Quaternion(Vector3.FORWARD, Vector3.BACK).get_euler()))\n```\n\noutput\n```\nBack->Forward:(0.0, 3.141593, 0.0)\nForward->Back:(0.0, 3.141593, 0.0)\nForward->Right:(0.0, -1.570796, 0.0)\nForward->Back:(0.0, 3.141593, 0.0)\nForward->Up:(1.570796, 0.0, 0.0)\nForward->Back:(0.0, 3.141593, 0.0)\n```\n\n\nHowever, as shown there, rotation around parallel axes is unstable.\n\nAt least GDScript prioritizes +Y in that case, but for those who want to prioritize +X, like in the Forward->Up example, +Y rotation means the rotation axis is unintended.\n\nWhile ensuring consistency with GDScript's behavior makes sense, but the common solution in such cases is for the user to detect whether the axes are parallel and provide a 180-degree rotation around any axis.\n\nIn other words, the inconsistency with GDScript can be attributed to C#, but from a broader perspective, it's likely a documentation issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643617062/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643799817","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113881#issuecomment-3643799817","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113881","id":3643799817,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZL_kJ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T21:12:05Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T21:38:44Z","body":"There shouldn't be an inconsistency with GDScript since the PR above, there used to be, but the changes brought the C# and GDScript code in alignment (if there's still cases where they don't align that should be fixed)\n\nBut indeed the edge case should be documented, but see also [this discussion](https://forum.godotengine.org/t/is-there-a-bug-in-quaternion-vector3-arcfrom-vector3-arcto/129407/8) which provides some hints on how to handle this case in a more predictable way\n\nBut indeed the mathematics here simply does not offer a clean solution, there are infinitely many equally \"correct\" results (or infinitely many equally \"incorrect\" results) and the engine picks one based on some conditions\n\nSo the specific logic and reasoning should be documented, making it clear that the case where the two vectors are collinear is degenerate and that the engine picks one based on a simple choice: cross product of the first vector with `Vector3.Right` if it is a valid option, otherwise with `Vector3.Up`","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643799817/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644801026","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113881#issuecomment-3644801026","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113881","id":3644801026,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZP0AC","user":{"login":"Supheria","id":77865986,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3ODY1OTg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77865986?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria","html_url":"https://github.com/Supheria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-12T03:57:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T03:57:24Z","body":"> However, as shown there, rotation around parallel axes is unstable.\n\nYes, you inspired me, and I found a solution two solve such problem.\n\nAs [normalized](https://forum.godotengine.org/t/is-there-a-bug-in-quaternion-vector3-arcfrom-vector3-arcto/129407/7?u=supheria) said, there are multi valid results mathematically, so the most “stable” way to create quaternion form an axis vector and a direction vector, is to judge two vectors parallel or not in first.\n\nIn C# code anyone can do like this ( in godot 4.5.1 mono ):\n\n``` c#\n// no need to normalize, \n// in 4.5.1 two vectors are both normalized in Quaternion construct function\nvar direction = new Vector(-1f, 0f, 0f); // use any value else\n\nvar axis = Vector3.Right;\n\n// if direction is parallel to axis, use another axis\nif (direction.Cross(axis).Length() == 0)\n{\n    axis = Vector3.Forward;\n}\n\nvar quaternion = new Quaternion(axis, direction);\n\n```\nThose who want to use Quaternion(Vector3 arcFrom, Vector3 arcTo) no matter in C# or GDScrpit can take reference in same.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644801026/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644809298","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113881#issuecomment-3644809298","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113881","id":3644809298,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZP2BS","user":{"login":"Supheria","id":77865986,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3ODY1OTg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77865986?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria","html_url":"https://github.com/Supheria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-12T04:02:11Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T04:02:11Z","body":"> 因此，具体的逻辑和推理应被记录下来，明确两个向量共线的情况是退化的，且引擎基于一个简单的选择选择：如果第一个向量有效，则乘积，否则`Vector3.Right``Vector3.Up`\n\nYes, it is useful to record such feature of quaternion in official document. Especially for those who accpt the suggestion in official document that quaternion is more powerful in rotation cast than Euler.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644809298/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644866574","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113881#issuecomment-3644866574","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113881","id":3644866574,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZQEAO","user":{"login":"Supheria","id":77865986,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3ODY1OTg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77865986?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria","html_url":"https://github.com/Supheria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-12T04:33:16Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T04:33:16Z","body":"By the way, rotation direction is not same exactly when axis judge oder is different.\n\n> `var axis = direction.Cross(Vector3.Right).Length() == 0 ? Vector3.Forward : Vector3.Right;`\n> <img width=\"583\" height=\"573\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d9c93f2-93e1-4dff-98ce-2ff673e94a94\" />\n\n\n\n> `var axis = direction.Cross(Vector3.Forward).Length() == 0 ? Vector3.Right : Vector3.Forward;`\n> <img width=\"566\" height=\"554\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e7eee55d-62fb-4caf-874c-af2d747bcc32\" />\n\n\n> the mesh:\n> <img width=\"430\" height=\"427\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a9157cd-3f4c-4a41-a04a-3ac91b671727\" />\n\n\nYou’d better make a test first if the rotation direction is required to be managed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644866574/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3645485506","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113881#issuecomment-3645485506","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113881","id":3645485506,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZSbHC","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","e